summary:
  A name the fold joined across its dots matches a stranger's plain first
  name anywhere in a credit.

history:
  "will.i.am" folds to "william" and took William Orbit's and William Bell's
  records; "t.A.T.u." folds to "tatu" and took Tatu Kantomaa's. A joined word
  meeting a plain one now counts like a short name.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SearchLogic.js

find:
          if (!mixed && letters(s) >= 4) return true;

replace:
          if (letters(s) >= 4) return true;

expect:
  Killed by tst_artpick::test_a_joined_up_name_is_no_strangers_first_name.
  Line-neutral.
